![kiss-bw](/wp-content/uploads/2013/11/kiss-bw-300x249.jpg)

Brothers and Sisters here is an epic tale like no other!

This is a dark love story between an American paramedic and a Russian debutante on the eve of a global revolution against the iron heel of the oligarchy.

A Futurist Noire set in a dystopian world of raw violent ambition, fearless loyalty, and belief in the things unseen; The Partizan Song is a four act work, the first in serial that combines fast paced multi character narrative with a veritable a laundry list of upcoming tactics for the militant human rights movement. It is a work on exploitation, grind house and agitprop linking its scope to an epic piece of 19th century Russian literature.

In the newly liberated Microrepublic of Breuklyn, there is great trouble brewing. Drones patrol the skies along the border and a new mile-high-wall has been built to prevent the traffic of people and contraband over the East River or Strong Island Sound into the United American States. Home to three million “stateless citizens”; this wild coastal gangland and nearly lawless rebel Free State is dominated by Irish and Italian municipal unions, Postsoviet and Haitian mobsters, Islamists, Messianic Hebrew cults, Black Nationalist guerrillas, Gypsy Partizans and a highly organized underground network known only by its clandestine acronym: the Z.O.B.\
Strange things are beginning to happen in this unrecognized pirate state. A tree of enormous size has grown as tall as a skyscraper in Prospect Park. Infants are being born who remember their past lives with remarkable detail. The various ultra-Orthodox cults of the Hassidim and Rastafarians have begun to nominate various pretenders to the role of Dror Ha Tzadikk; Messianic candidate of the generation. An uneasy alliance between the West Indians, and the Jews brokered by the factions of the resistance is about to erupt in all out violence after a mysterious and grisly series of group killings.

Life has taken on a highly libertarian, yet libertine state of emergency.

After waging a three year bloody separatist war and securing their borders with miracles, the secrets of parapsychology as well as New York Native grit; a small zealous band of rebels has set their eyes on the liberation of a war torn African country named Sudan to export the Human Rights Revolution of the Great Revolt.

On the eve of the January 1st, marking the anniversary of the Haitian Revolution of 1804 a small band of Partizan fighters have planned to invade Africa’s largest nation Sudan, where President for life Omar Al Bashir is preoccupied carrying out a long running genocide. The rebels plan to liberate Africa and set off a chain reaction of events to bring the world’s war criminals and oligarchs to their knees.

